hadiths[18]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2116","Amir bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas narrated from his father"
"2117","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:""Indeed a man"
"2118","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:""It is not right for a Muslim man to spend two nights"
"2119","Talhah bin Musarrif said:""I said to Ibn Abi Awfi: Did the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) leave a will?' He said: 'No' I said: 'How is the will written"
"2120","Abu Ummah said:""During the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage"
"2121","Amr bin Kharajah narrated:""The Prophet (s.a.w) gave a Khutbah upon his she-camel"
"2122","Al-Harith narrated from 'Ali:""The Prophet (s.a.w) judged with the debt before the will"
"2123","Abu Habibah At-Ta'i said:""My brother willed a portion of his wealth to me. So I met Abu Ad-Darda and said: 'My brother has willed a portion of his wealth to me"
"2124","Urwah narrated that :'Aishah had informed him that Barrirah came to her ('Aishah) seeking her help for her writ of emancipation"
"2183","Hudhaifah bin Asid said:""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) stood over us on a balcony"
"2184","Safiyyah narrated ""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:'The people will not finish attacking this House until it is attacked by an army which"
"2185","Aishah narrated ""The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:'In the end of this Ummah there will be a collapse"
"2186","Abu Dharr said:""I entered the Masjid at sunset"
"2187","Zainab bint Jahsh said:""One day the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) awoke from sleep with a flushed red face"
"2188","Abdullah [bin Mas'ud] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""In the end of time there will come a people young in years"
"2189","Usaid bin Hudair said:""A man from Ansar said"
"2190","Abdullah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:""Indeed"
"2191","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:""One day"